! ---------------------------------------------------------------------- !
! DRAFT -- secofs_ufs_ww3 -- companion "GRID%NML" auxiliary namelist for !
! ww3_grid.nml (implicit-PDLIB solver flags). NOT one of the 6 requested !
! deliverables -- added because ww3_grid.nml's GRID%NML pointer would be !
! non-functional without it. See DECISIONS.txt.                          !
!                                                                        !
! SOURCE (real file, verbatim structure/flags):                          !
!   WW3/regtests/ww3_tp2.6/input/                !
!     namelists_pdlib.nml (implicit PDLIB: IMPFSN family, JGS_* Gauss-   !
!     Seidel solver params)                                              !
! Contrast source (explicit PDLIB, NOT used here -- task specifies       !
! "implicit PDLIB"):                                                     !
!   WW3/regtests/ww3_ufs1.1/input_unstr/        !
!     namelists_a.nml (EXPFSN=T / IMPFSN=F)                              !
!                                                                        !
! This file's &UNST group is a DIFFERENT namelist from ww3_grid.nml's    !
! own UNST_NML despite the shared name "UNST" -- WW3's legacy-style      !
! (non-slash-terminated single-line) namelist for solver/physics flags   !
! referenced via GRID%NML, vs. the modern UNST_NML mesh-file block       !
! inside ww3_grid.nml itself. Both real references above use exactly     !
! this split.                                                            !
!                                                                        !
! UGOBCAUTO=F (matches both real references): boundary nodes are NOT     !
! auto-detected from the mesh; they must be supplied via the             !
! INBND_POINT_NML block in ww3_grid.nml. UGOBCFILE (an alternative to    !
! per-point INBND_POINT_NML -- a standalone boundary-node-list file) is  !
! NOT set here; we default to the INBND_POINT_NML path since that is     !
! what both real references do. If the mesh-tooling output instead       !
! produces a ready-made boundary file, switching to UGOBCFILE='<path>'   !
! is the lower-effort alternative -- flagged as an open choice in        !
! DECISIONS.txt, not decided here.                                       !
!                                                                        !
! JGS_* (Jacobi/Gauss-Seidel implicit solver control) and IMP* flags     !
! below are copied VERBATIM from the real ww3_tp2.6 implicit-PDLIB       !
! reference -- these are generic WW3 solver-tuning defaults, not         !
! SECOFS-specific, and are a reasonable starting point pending WCOSS2    !
! convergence testing on the actual SECOFS wave mesh. UNVERIFIED for     !
! SECOFS scale specifically (tp2.6 is a small nearshore test mesh).      !
! ---------------------------------------------------------------------- !

&UNST UGOBCAUTO = F,
UGOBCDEPTH= -10.,
EXPFSN = F,
EXPFSPSI = F,
EXPFSFCT = F,
IMPFSN = F,
EXPTOTAL = F,
IMPTOTAL = T,
IMPREFRACTION = T,
IMPFREQSHIFT = T,
IMPSOURCE = T,
SETUP_APPLY_WLV = F,
SOLVERTHR_SETUP=1E-14,
CRIT_DEP_SETUP=0.1,
JGS_USE_JACOBI = T,
JGS_BLOCK_GAUSS_SEIDEL = T,
JGS_TERMINATE_MAXITER = T,
JGS_MAXITER = 1000,
JGS_TERMINATE_NORM = F,
JGS_TERMINATE_DIFFERENCE = T,
JGS_DIFF_THR = 1.E-8,
JGS_PMIN = 3.0,
JGS_LIMITER = T,
JGS_NORM_THR = 1.E-20 /
END OF NAMELISTS
